            </PageCard>

            <PageCard Title="8. Build your Tailwind CSS">
                <p Class="mb-3">
                    Install the <a href="https://tailwindcss.com/docs/installation/tailwind-cli" target="_blank">Tailwind CLI</a> from the solution root - the outer <code>{YourProjectName}</code> folder that contains both <code>{YourProjectName}/</code> and <code>{YourProjectName}.Client/</code>:
                </p>
                <TwCodeBlock Content="@wasmTailwindInstall" Language="bash" />
                <p Class="my-3">
                    Create an input stylesheet at <code>{YourProjectName}/wwwroot/css/input.css</code>. It lives in the host project, since that's what App.razor's <code>&lt;link&gt;</code> tag references, but its <code>@@source</code> directives need to reach into <code>{YourProjectName}.Client</code> too, because that's where MainLayout.razor and Theme.cs live. The keyframes at the bottom power <code>TwSkeleton</code>'s <code>Wave</code> variant - a shimmer effect Tailwind has no utility for, so it has to be real CSS rather than a class Tailwind can generate. Skip it if you don't use that variant:
                </p>
                <TwCodeBlock Content="@wasmTailwindInput" Language="css" />
                <p Class="my-3">
                    Then build it to <code>{YourProjectName}/wwwroot/css/output.css</code>, the file already referenced by the <code>&lt;link&gt;</code> tag you added to App.razor in step 3:
                </p>
                <TwCodeBlock Content="@wasmTailwindBuild" Language="bash" />
            </PageCard>

            <PageCard Title="9. Try it out">
                <p Class="mb-3">
                    Add a test page to confirm everything is wired up. Since it needs to be interactive under WebAssembly, it has to live in the Client project. Create <code>{YourProjectName}.Client/Pages/ComponentTest.razor</code>:
                </p>
                <ExampleCodeBlock Razor="@wasmComponentTestPageRazor" CSharp="@wasmComponentTestPageCode" />
                <p Class="my-3">
                    Run the app and go to <code>/component-test</code>. You should see a green success alert, a button whose label counts up each click, and three interactive switches.
                </p>
            </PageCard>
        </TwTab>


